The Canadian Institute of Cybersecurity (CIC) has created the CICIDS2017 data set which is one of the most popular
benchmarks sets for testing Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) in traditional network environments. 
It was designed to overcome the drawbacks of previous datasets (KDD'99, NSL-KDD) by adding realistic background network traffic and 
contemporary cyber attack scenarios. The dataset is made up of 5 days of normal and malicious network traffic with different categories of
attacks such as Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS), Brute Force Attacks, Infiltration, Web Based Attacks, and Botnet activity. 
